export default {"id":"production-level-14","number":14,"title":"Module 14 — Capstones F and G","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"1. Deliverable 3 (Remix): Must preserve a recognizable Key Element (usually the lead vocal topline) so an independent listener can immediately name the original song. 2. Deliverable 4 (Flip): Treats source audio as raw material sliced into ","modules":[{"id":"production-m-14-1","code":"14","title":"Remix and Flip Capstones (Deliverables 3 & 4 · Gates F and G)","blurb":"1. Deliverable 3 (Remix): Must preserve a recognizable Key Element (usually the lead vocal topline) so an independent listener can immediately name the original song. 2. Deliverable 4 (Flip): Treats source audio as raw material sliced into ","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"production-l-o-19","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 14 — Remix and Flip Capstones (Deliverables 3 & 4 · Gates F and G)","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Intent:</strong> Complete both required transformational capstones: <strong>Deliverable 3 (The Identifiable Remix · Gate F)</strong> and <strong>Deliverable 4 (The Deconstructed Flip · Gate G)</strong>. Both pieces are mandatory curriculum requirements. Neither piece may substitute for the other. Export 24-bit lossless master WAVs for both projects, maintain strict source provenance documentation, and achieve <strong>Gates F and G Certification</strong>.   <strong>Required Capstone Module.</strong> Gates F and G.   <strong>Strict Pedagogical Invariants:</strong>  "},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Deliverable 3 (Remix)</strong>: Must preserve a recognizable Key Element (usually the lead vocal topline) so an independent listener can immediately name the original song.","<strong>Deliverable 4 (Flip)</strong>: Treats source audio as raw material sliced into 16 Drum Rack pads; original identity is dismantled into a new original composition.","Both deliverables must be independent Live projects collected and saved into their own dedicated folders.  "],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Primary Source References:</strong> EDMProd (<em>How to Remix a Song</em> / Sam Matla); <em>The Ultimate Remix Guide.pdf</em>; <em>How to Sample Sounds A Beginners Guide for Music Producers</em>; <em>Drum Breaks_ A Guide To Injecting Character into Your Music.pdf</em>; Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual (Ch. 9: Warping, Ch. 13: Slicing, Ch. 34: Exporting); <em>Song Finishing Checklist.pdf</em>."},{"type":"heading","text":"Section 14.1 — Deliverable 3: The Remix","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section ID:</strong> <code>production-m14-1</code>   <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Ingest, warp, and align legal multi-track stems in Ableton Live 12 Standard.","Implement one named EDMProd remix architecture (e.g., Re-Harmonization, Genre Translation, Structural Inversion).","Enforce the Key Element Anchor (preserving vocal topline recognizability).","Produce 100% original drums, bass, and chords in Live 12 Standard.","Construct a full 32–64+ bar arrangement (2.0–3.5 minutes).","Export a 24-bit lossless master WAV with POW-r 3 dither and achieve <strong>Gate F Certification</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-1","title":"14.1.1 — Selecting the Remix Source Material","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.1 — Selecting the Remix Source Material","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Ingest authorized multi-track stems with clear vocal headroom.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Selection Standards","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Select an authorized remix contest stem pack, royalty-free vocal library kit, or cleared commercial stem set."},{"type":"list","items":["The source must feature a compelling, clean lead vocal topline or distinct melodic hook that will serve as the recognizable anchor of your remix."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-2","title":"14.1.2 — Confirming Source Provenance in Writing","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.2 — Confirming Source Provenance in Writing","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Document legal licensing terms and stem origin in project notes.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Provenance Logging","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Create <code>SOURCE_LOG.txt</code> in <code>Deliverable_3_Remix_Project/</code>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">===================================================================\nDELIVERABLE 3: REMIX SOURCE PROVENANCE LOG\n===================================================================\n- Song Title: \"Summer Horizon\"\n- Original Artist: Jane Doe\n- Origin / Source: Official Metapop/Splice Remix Contest\n- Licensing Agreement: Cleared for Educational Non-Commercial Production\n- Stems Utilized: Lead_Vocal_Dry.wav, Lead_Vocal_Harmonies.wav\n- Stems Discarded: 14 Original Drum, Bass, and Synth Stems\n- Original Tempo: 82.00 BPM | Remix Tempo: 126.00 BPM\n===================================================================</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-3","title":"14.1.3 — Naming and Committing to Your Remix Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.3 — Naming and Committing to Your Remix Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Execute one of the six canonical EDMProd approaches.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. The Methodological Selection","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Commit in writing to your primary remix architecture:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Approach 1 (Re-Harmonization)</strong>: New chords under unchanged vocal.","<strong>Approach 2 (Genre Translation)</strong>: Transforming a ballad into a 126 BPM club track.","<strong>Approach 5 (Structural Inversion)</strong>: Dropping where they broke down."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-4","title":"14.1.4 — Protecting the Key Element Anchor","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.4 — Protecting the Key Element Anchor","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Ensure that vocal topline intelligibility and melodic identity remain intact.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. The Recognizability Invariant","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Keep the lead vocal acapella prominently featured in the mix:"},{"type":"list","items":["Do NOT drown the vocal in massive third-party distortion or over-slice it into micro-glitches.","High-pass filter supporting synthesizers and pads at 250 Hz to leave the low-mid vocal fundamental clear."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-5","title":"14.1.5 — Arranging a Full 32–64+ Bar Song Form","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.5 — Arranging a Full 32–64+ Bar Song Form","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Construct a complete musical journey rather than a static loop.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Complete Remix Roadmap","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Scaffold the timeline with named Locators: <code>01_Remix_Intro (8–16b)</code>  <code>02_Verse_1 (16b)</code>  <code>03_Build (8b)</code>  <code>04_MAIN_REMIX_DROP (16–32b)</code>  <code>05_Breakdown (8–16b)</code>  <code>06_DROP_2_CLIMAX (16–32b)</code>  <code>07_Outro (8–16b)</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-6","title":"14.1.6 — Performing from Launchkey MK4 or Printing on the Ruler","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.6 — Performing from Launchkey MK4 or Printing on the Ruler","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Execute the remix arrangement pass via hardware scenes or linear editing.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Production Execution","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Option A (Launchkey MK4 Scene Pass)</strong>: Trigger remix scenes live using MK4 RGB pads, recording the performance onto the timeline.","<strong>Option B (Linear Arrangement Writing)</strong>: Sculpt the arrangement directly on the horizontal ruler."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-7","title":"14.1.7 — Exporting the Lossless Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.7 — Exporting the Lossless Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Render the final 24-bit master bounce in Live 12 Standard.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Master Audio Render Configuration (Ctrl + Shift + R)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Render Track</strong>: <code>Master</code>","<strong>File Type</strong>: <code>WAV</code> | <strong>Sample Rate</strong>: <code>44100 Hz</code> | <strong>Bit Depth</strong>: <code>24</code>","<strong>Dither</strong>: <code>POW-r 3</code> | <strong>Normalize</strong>: <code>Off</code>","<strong>Output File</strong>: <code>Deliverable_3_Remix_Master_v01.wav</code>"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-8","title":"14.1.8 — The Written Remix Identity Audit","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.8 — The Written Remix Identity Audit","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Document what remains of the original song in project notes.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Written Attestation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Document in <code>REMIX_AUDIT.txt</code>:"},{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"<em>\"What remains of the original song is the complete, unedited lead vocal topline in Chorus 1 and Chorus 2. All drums, basslines, chord progressions, and transitional sweeps are 100% newly authored in Live 12 Standard.\"</em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-9","title":"14.1.9 — Methodological Critique","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.9 — Methodological Critique","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Verify compliance with the Stem Economy Rule and early arrangement discipline.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Self-Audit","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Confirm that you discarded at least 70% of provided stems and arranged the full song timeline before fine-tuning mixing plugins."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-1-10","title":"14.1.10 — Collect All and Save & Gate F Certification","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.10 — Collect All and Save & Gate F Certification","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Archive the project and attain Gate F Certification.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Project Archival","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Execute <code>File -&gt; Collect All and Save</code> into <code>Deliverable_3_Remix_Project/</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-gate-f","title":"F — Deliverable 3 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"F — Deliverable 3 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>1. Complete Project Directory</strong>: <code>Deliverable_3_Remix_Project/</code> with collected <code>.als</code> Set.","[ ] <strong>2. Exported 24-Bit Master WAV</strong>: <code>Deliverable_3_Remix_Master_v01.wav</code> (&gt; 2.0 minutes, no clipping, 44.1 kHz / 24-bit / POW-r 3).","[ ] <strong>3. Written Source Provenance Log</strong>: <code>SOURCE_LOG.txt</code> documenting legal origin and stems ingested.","[ ] <strong>4. Strangers' Identity Test</strong>: Verified confirmation that an independent listener can name the original song."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-1","title":"14.2.1 — Selecting the Flip Source Phrase","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.1 — Selecting the Flip Source Phrase","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Choose an authorized, owned, or royalty-free phrase for granular slicing.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Target Phrase Selection","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Select an authorized 2-bar or 4-bar phrase (a vintage electric piano chord progression, a clean brass horn lick, or an expressive vocal run)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-2","title":"14.2.2 — Confirming Source Provenance in Writing","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.2 — Confirming Source Provenance in Writing","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Maintain copyright provenance integrity for physical sampling assets.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Legal Logging","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Create <code>SOURCE_LOG.txt</code> in <code>Deliverable_4_Flip_Project/</code> documenting sample origin and licensing terms."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-3","title":"14.2.3 — Slicing Phrase to 16 Drum Rack Pads","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.3 — Slicing Phrase to 16 Drum Rack Pads","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Populate Drum Rack pads 1–16 using Live's slicing engine.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Slicing Protocol","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Right-click audio clip  <strong>Slice to New MIDI Track</strong>  Preset: <code>Built-in Slicing Preset</code>. Slices populate pads 1–16."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-4","title":"14.2.4 — Re-Sequencing a Completely New Identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.4 — Re-Sequencing a Completely New Identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Deconstruct chronological order, transpose slices, and establish a new motif.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Deconstruction Mechanics","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Set all Drum Rack pads to <strong>Choke Group 1</strong>.","Pitch Pad 4 up +5 st; reverse Pad 8.","Tap pads in a completely new order (5 2 11 1) to generate an original musical hook."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-5","title":"14.2.5 — Writing Original Harmony Under the Sliver","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.5 — Writing Original Harmony Under the Sliver","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Compose new bass and chord layers underneath sliced audio fragments.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Harmonic Layering","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Load <strong>Drift</strong> or <strong>Electric</strong> on Track 2 and 3. Compose a 4-bar chord progression and sub-bassline that re-harmonizes the sliced chop motif."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-6","title":"14.2.6 — Arranging a Full 32–64+ Bar Flip Form","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.6 — Arranging a Full 32–64+ Bar Flip Form","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Construct a complete linear arrangement for the flip.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Flip Timeline Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<code>01_Flip_Intro (8b)</code>  <code>02_Chop_Verse (16b)</code>  <code>03_Build (8b)</code>  <code>04_MAIN_FLIP_DROP (16–32b)</code>  <code>05_Outro (8b)</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-7","title":"14.2.7 — Performing from Launchkey MK4 Pads (Channel 10, Notes 36–51)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.7 — Performing from Launchkey MK4 Pads (Channel 10, Notes 36–51)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Capture live expressive finger-drumming performances.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Hardware Performance Capture","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Set Launchkey MK4 to <strong>Drum Mode</strong>. Perform the chop rhythm live and record the MIDI pass directly into the Arrangement timeline."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-8","title":"14.2.8 — Exporting the Lossless Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.8 — Exporting the Lossless Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Render the final 24-bit master bounce in Live 12 Standard.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Master Audio Render Configuration (Ctrl + Shift + R)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Render Track</strong>: <code>Master</code>","<strong>File Type</strong>: <code>WAV</code> | <strong>Sample Rate</strong>: <code>44100 Hz</code> | <strong>Bit Depth</strong>: <code>24</code>","<strong>Dither</strong>: <code>POW-r 3</code> | <strong>Normalize</strong>: <code>Off</code>","<strong>Output File</strong>: <code>Deliverable_4_Flip_Master_v01.wav</code>"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-9","title":"14.2.9 — The Written Deconstruction Audit","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.9 — The Written Deconstruction Audit","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Attest that original song identity has been dismantled into raw material.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Written Attestation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Document in <code>FLIP_AUDIT.txt</code>:"},{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"<em>\"The original source audio was sliced into 16 Drum Rack pads, repitched, choked, and re-sequenced. An independent listener cannot identify the original recording. The audio serves strictly as a new original granular instrument.\"</em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l14-2-10","title":"14.2.10 — Collect All and Save & Gate G Certification","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.10 — Collect All and Save & Gate G Certification","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Archive the project and attain Gate G Certification.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Project Archival","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Execute <code>File -&gt; Collect All and Save</code> into <code>Deliverable_4_Flip_Project/</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-gate-g","title":"G — Deliverable 4 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"G — Deliverable 4 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>1. Complete Project Directory</strong>: <code>Deliverable_4_Flip_Project/</code> with collected <code>.als</code> Set.","[ ] <strong>2. Exported 24-Bit Master WAV</strong>: <code>Deliverable_4_Flip_Master_v01.wav</code> (&gt; 90 seconds, no clipping, 44.1 kHz / 24-bit / POW-r 3).","[ ] <strong>3. Drum Rack Chops Verification</strong>: Verified Drum Rack on Channel 10 triggering granular slices.","[ ] <strong>4. Deconstruction Attestation</strong>: <code>FLIP_AUDIT.txt</code> documenting sample transformation."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
